# Expectation record for 03_initializers/003_partial_zero_fill.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 003_partial_zero_fill
area               = 03_initializers
description        = Implicit zero fill of every member and element left unmentioned by an initializer and of every static object declared without one, across nine partial and designated situations plus automatic-duration twins, each slot read back individually; the positional partial STRUCT spelling is excluded, narrowly and with its reason recorded in impl_defined_notes, because the frozen warning gate rejects every spelling of it
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined and no unspecified behaviour, which is the precondition that
makes both differential oracles sound: undefined behaviour would license either compiler to do
anything at all, so a divergence over it would prove nothing about either one.
THE ZERO GUARANTEE IS THE SUBJECT OF THIS PROGRAM RATHER THAN AN INCIDENTAL PROPERTY, so it is
stated first, and it is also the point this program looks most likely to violate, because it
prints values nothing in the source ever stores. NOTHING HERE READS UNINITIALIZED STORAGE.
g_noinit and the two unmentioned elements of g_ptrs have STATIC storage duration, and C11
6.7.9p10 defines the contents of an object of static storage duration with no initializer as zero
for an arithmetic type and a null pointer for a pointer type -- definite values, not indeterminate
ones. The elements and members left unmentioned by a partial initializer are likewise defined as
initialized to zero by C11 6.7.9p19 and 6.7.9p21, and that applies to the automatic-duration
objects exactly as it does to the static ones, because an object with ANY initializer is fully
initialized. Every automatic object in main -- l_arr, l_all_zero, l_zero_struct, l_part, l_arr_st
and l_matrix -- carries an initializer, so none of them holds
an indeterminate value at any point. The program asserts an OMISSION rather than a store: nothing
here writes the zeros it prints, so a slot that came back non-zero would mean the compiler failed
to supply a guarantee the source never spelled out. The guarantee is the standard's, not an
assumption of the test's.
No arithmetic is performed on the data, so no signed overflow is reachable; the only arithmetic is
the loop counters' increments, bounded by the literals 6, 4, 3 and 2. Nothing is shifted, divided
or remaindered. Nothing is modified after its initialization, so no object is modified twice
between two sequence points.
Every subscript stays strictly inside its array bound, and each bound is a literal matching the
declared extent: g_arr and l_arr are int[6] read at 0 through 5, g_all_zero, l_all_zero and g_uarr
are 4 elements read at 0 through 3, g_arr_st and l_arr_st are struct inner[3] read at 0 through 2,
g_matrix and l_matrix are int[2][3] read at [0..1][0..2], g_noinit is int[3] read at 0 through 2,
and g_ptrs is 3 elements read at 0 through 2. No one-past-the-end pointer is formed.
The pointer array is the only place a pointer appears. g_ptrs[0] points at the string literal
"first", whose array has 6 elements, and only index 0 of it is read; no string literal is written
through. g_ptrs[1] and g_ptrs[2] are compared against 0 as a null-or-not predicate and are NEVER
dereferenced. No pointer VALUE is printed, no pointer difference is taken and no pointer arithmetic
beyond that in-bounds read is performed.
There is no aliasing violation: every value is read through an lvalue of its own declared type --
int through int, unsigned through unsigned, and the string literal's element through char, narrowed
by an explicit (unsigned char) cast which is a value conversion rather than a reinterpretation. No
object representation is examined, no union appears, and no pointer is cast to a different object
pointer type. Only named members and elements are read, never a padding byte: the { 0 } idiom
guarantees each MEMBER is zero and says nothing about padding, whose contents are unspecified, and
this program never inspects a representation, so that distinction cannot bite. Nothing depends on
the relative addresses of unrelated objects.
Every initializer value is small and positive -- the largest is 82 and the widest is 7u -- so each
is representable in the type it initializes and no implicit conversion changes a value.
Each printf call receives at most one loop counter and one datum, neither of which has a side
effect, so the unspecified order in which a function call's arguments are evaluated cannot be
observed. Every conversion specifier matches its argument after the default argument promotions:
%d takes int -- including the two ?: expressions, whose operands are the int constants 1 and 0, and
the (int)(unsigned char) narrowing -- and %u takes unsigned int. Both types are four bytes on all
four targets, so no variadic argument is read at the wrong width.
main returns 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is truncated by
the operating system. Nothing outside this file is read: every input is a literal here, no file,
socket, environment variable, clock, random source or locale is consulted, and iteration order is
fixed by literal loop bounds, so every cell is reproducible from this source and this record alone.
No header is included anywhere and printf is declared by hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`.
bcc bundles the nine required freestanding headers plus a bonus stdatomic.h and ships no standard
I/O header (docs/project-guide.md line 212), so naming one would fail on the bcc side of oracle (a)
while succeeding on the reference side -- a spurious divergence caused by the test rather than by a
compiler. This area is granted no header exception; the corpus has exactly two, area 07's stdarg.h
and the dedicated bundled-header probe in area 12.
This record declares no warning-gate deviation, and area 03 sanctions none. The program is clean
under the full default gate -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow
-Werror at -O0, -O1 and -O2 with all four reference drivers, with no diagnostic of any kind and no
source-level diagnostic suppression anywhere in the translation unit, and it builds and runs clean
under the sanitizer gate -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all. Both gates are
reference-compiler-only and are never applied to bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is
untouched. One initializer spelling is excluded to reach that clean audit rather than suppressed
inside it, and the exclusion, its measured reason and what the zero guarantee retains regardless
are recorded in impl_defined_notes below.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This record narrows nothing that the harness reads: all four targets, all three optimization
levels and all three oracles are enabled, no expected-divergence marker is carried, no gate
deviation is claimed under the ub_audit_flags key, and no implementation-defined value reaches
this program's output. One initializer SPELLING is nevertheless excluded from the source, and the
paragraph below states which, why, and what the zero guarantee retains regardless.
CONSTRAINT-C3 EXCLUSION -- THE POSITIONAL PARTIAL STRUCT SPELLING. `struct outer v = { 1 };`,
which supplies the leading members POSITIONALLY and leaves the rest to the zero guarantee, is
well-defined C11 (6.7.9p19 and p21), and it is a materially different route through the
initializer walker than `{ .tag = 1 }`: the designated form repositions the cursor explicitly,
whereas the positional form relies on the cursor stopping where the list runs out. GCC
nevertheless reports it under -Wmissing-field-initializers, which -Wextra enables and which the
audit gate's -Werror makes fatal -- the diagnostic reports the very guarantee under test.
Sixteen spellings were MEASURED against that gate with the reference compiler, and the positional
partial STRUCT is the only shape it rejects; it rejects every variant of that shape, so no
spelling of that particular route exists that the unmodified gate accepts. No admissible deviation
exists either: the gate's removable members are exactly -pedantic, for the GCC-extensions area, and
-Wconversion with -Wsign-conversion, for the deliberate narrowing program, so -Wextra is not
removable and area 03 is granted no deviation at all. A source-level diagnostic-suppression
directive is not an alternative to that: it neutralizes a gate member from inside the translation
unit while this record still claims the unchanged gate, which would make this record's own claim
false rather than making the program clean. The spelling is therefore dropped from the source, and
constraint C3 is satisfied the way it asks to be -- the exclusion is narrow, it is scoped to one
spelling, it changes no target, no optimization level and no oracle, and its reason is recorded here
and in the program's own header comment. The specific loss is the positional-cursor route through a
STRUCT, at the three descent depths and in the array-of-struct-element form the excluded objects
used to cover; that loss is stated rather than left to be inferred.
THE ZERO GUARANTEE ITSELF LOSES NOTHING, which is what keeps the exclusion narrow. The same
measurement established that -Wmissing-field-initializers does NOT fire for a designated
initializer, nor for the `= { 0 }` idiom, nor for a partial ARRAY, nor for a partial
array-of-struct, nor for partial two-dimensional rows -- GCC treats the all-zero idiom as
intentional and treats element omission as unremarkable -- so all nine zero-fill situations, which
are the whole of this program's mandate, are written plainly and all remain under test. Positional
exhaustion is itself still exercised here: g_arr and l_arr are int[6] = { 1, 2 }, which the gate
accepts unaided because -Wmissing-field-initializers is about members rather than elements, so the
cursor-runs-out path is covered for elements even though it is no longer covered for members. The
nearest gate-clean relative of the excluded spelling, a designator followed by positional
continuation, is covered in 006_designated_mixed_nested.c, which spells { 1, { .q = 3 }, 4 } and
{ .tag = 11, { .p = 12, .q = 13 }, 14 }.
EXECUTION CHARACTER SET, PINNED AT TRANSLATION TIME. One printed value is the numeric code of the
'f' in "first", and C11 5.2.1 leaves the values of the execution character set to the
implementation. The source asserts `'f' == 102` with _Static_assert, so an implementation with a
different execution character set fails to TRANSLATE rather than printing a different number that
an oracle would have to attribute to a compiler defect. All four supported targets were measured
to use ASCII. Verified by negative test: changing the asserted value makes translation fail.
WIDTH NORMALIZATION. Only int, unsigned int and const char * appear, and the pointers are never
printed as values -- only as a null-or-not predicate and as a character read through them -- so
nothing depends on a width that differs across the targets: a pointer and the integer type that
matches it are four bytes on i686 where the other three targets make them eight
(docs/technical-specifications.md target table, lines 457-462), a difference also MEASURED on all
four targets in this environment. No long, size_t, ptrdiff_t or floating value reaches a format
string, no sizeof and no _Alignof result is printed, and no address is printed. Where the
implementation places these objects, and whether two identical string literals share storage, is
left entirely free: no address is printed and no two pointers are compared for identity.
PLAIN-CHAR SIGNEDNESS. The one character read from a string literal is normalized through
(int)(unsigned char), so the MEASURED signedness of plain char -- signed on x86-64 and i686,
unsigned on AArch64 and RISC-V 64 -- cannot reach the output.
PADDING. Only named members are read: the { 0 } idiom guarantees each member is zero and says
nothing about padding bytes, and this program never inspects a representation, so the distinction
cannot bite.
THE DISCRIMINATING VARIANT. Nine distinct zero-fill situations are read back slot by slot, and the
automatic-duration twins carry the most weight in this program, which is why all three optimization
levels matter. A static object's zeros come from the image the linker emits -- the wholly zero
objects g_all_zero, g_zero_struct and g_noinit reach BSS while the partially initialized ones carry
literal zero bytes in the data section, both placements confirmed at -O0 on all four targets --
whereas an automatic object's zeros must be produced by instructions the backend emits on entry to
the block. A compiler can implement one correctly and the other incorrectly, and only holding both
forms side by side distinguishes the two. The level is named because the placement is a property of
that one level rather than of all three: at -O1 and -O2, on all four targets, the reference compiler
was measured to prove that nothing writes any of these objects and to act on it -- only g_arr and
g_arr_st survive, moved to READ-ONLY data and still read from there through their loops, while every
other one of them is eliminated outright with its reads folded to immediates. A reader who
reproduces the section placement at -O2 therefore will not find the -O0 answer, and that is the
implementation's freedom rather than this record being wrong. It is also exactly why the sweep covers
-O0, -O1 and -O2 rather than one level: the VALUES read back may not change however the
initialization is realized, and those values are the only thing the three oracles compare.
MEASURED EVIDENCE. The program was compiled with the reference driver for all four targets at -O0,
-O1 and -O2 -- twelve configurations -- and every one produced these 75 lines byte-identically
with exit status 0, which is why oracle (b) compares this program's targets against each other
without any narrowing and why oracle (c) can hold these bytes as the golden record. The same
twelve configurations were re-measured after the excluded spelling was removed, so the 75 lines
below are the current source's output rather than a residue of an earlier one. The output is a
fixed sequence of 75 key=value lines, one per property claimed and nothing summarized, so one
divergent line localizes the defect to one zero-fill situation.
END
